# Dashboard appifact — shared type

This page is the Dashboard RUNTIME only: index.html, artifact-type/app.js,
artifact-type/capture.js (loaded instead of app.js to picture a dashboard),
artifact-type/app.css and
artifact-type/thumbnail/thumbnail.json (which of a dashboard's documents the
platform reads to picture it on the Artifacts page) are the
type's runtime, published with each release and shared by every dashboard
built on it. Nothing about any particular dashboard is in these files.

## Where a dashboard's data lives

In the dashboard's own live store (the db capability), never in a file:
dash/meta {title, lang?}, dash/params {name: default} for the {{name}}s its queries
take, dash/look (a design system's colors, type and corners), one
datasets/<id> per dataset and one files/<name> {text}
per file of its page (index.html, and any .css or .js it names): plain
HTML, CSS and JS, since the type draws no components of its own and styles
just two classes for a page, `dash-skeleton` and `dash-select`. Only
people who can edit the dashboard can write any of it (the type's db rules). A
query dataset carries only one tool call (connector, tool, arguments) — every viewer runs it with their own access, unless someone shares its connector: then it runs with that person's access and its results are stored in the dashboard. Otherwise its rows are not in the store (that
viewer's own browser keeps a query's last answer for up to a week), but for what
an editor's page shows of them while Claude works beside it, in their own part. The page's files are
code an editor wrote, and the type mounts and runs them in its own document, as
an artifact runs what its editors publish; a script or stylesheet tag that is
not one of those files is dropped from the markup (d3 ships with the type).
See SKILL.md.
